course: dictionary
lesson: 8033
title: Refugee: someone who had to flee
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A refugee is a person who has had to leave their home country because of war, danger or cruel treatment, and has gone somewhere safer. The key idea is the reason: a refugee did not leave for a holiday or a new job, but because they had to stay safe.
explain: «A refugee is someone who had to leave their country to be safe, for example because of war.» The clues are had to and to be safe. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "A refugee is someone who went on holiday to be safe" does not make sense, so holiday is wrong.
explain: Refugee is a noun, and its plural is refugees. The word can also be used more loosely, as in «refugees from the flood», meaning people who had to escape from a place, not only from a country.
explain: Compare refugee with migrant. «A migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life.» Both people move somewhere new, so the reason for leaving is the clue that tells them apart.
fact: A refugee fled war or danger to their life.
fact: A migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life; a refugee has to leave to be safe.
fact: «Refugee camp» is a place where refugees may live for a time, and some camps hold hundreds of thousands of people for years.
fact: The UN refugee agency, UNHCR, runs or supports many refugee camps.
exercise: «A refugee is someone who had to leave their country to be safe.» Who is a refugee? | A man who moved abroad for a new job | A football fan travelling to a match | A child who went on a holiday abroad | *A family who fled a war to stay safe
exercise: «Refugee camps can hold hundreds of thousands of people for years.» What does refugee camp suggest? | A shop that sells tents | A holiday park by the sea | A school for young footballers | *A place where refugees live, sometimes for a long time
exercise: Maya says a migrant and a refugee are the same. What is the real difference? | A refugee moves for work; a migrant had to flee a war | Only refugees are allowed to cross borders | *A refugee had to leave to be safe; a migrant moved, often for work or a better life | They mean exactly the same thing
test: In «refugees from the flood», what does refugees mean? | People who built the flood defences | *People who had to escape from the flood | People who swim every day | People who sell water
test: Which word in «He fled his town when the fighting started» shows that he had to escape? | when | town | started | *fled
exam: Which sentence uses refugee correctly? | We went to the refugee for a sunny holiday. | The refugee won the school sports day race. | The refugee painted a bright red fence. | *After the war, the family became refugees in a safer country.
